{"baseRefName":"codex/parallax-surface-orientation","body":"Administrators can connect AI spending to capabilities, provider attempts and genuinely useful room acceptance or Assistant Apply through the existing Admiralty workspace. The update adds precise versioned accounting, failed-attempt exposure, safe history/inspection, effective person allowances and audited capability/pricing controls. Daily UTC request cohorts compare acceptance/Apply rates and cost per useful result. Quality separately reports logical operations and provider attempts per useful result: the synthetic Assistant cohort shows 1.14 versus 1.19, while incomplete capture leaves provider efficiency unavailable with explicit coverage. Parallax retains execution, accounting and canonical-save authority.\n\nDevelopment verification passes 138 focused cases across ten files and 102 Sounding Line regression checks. Frozen product source `4a185cbf6ba04c25564dcb5d031f03ef588de3c4` passes two complete actual desktop/mobile production-browser journeys with 32 fresh captures, two recordings and 12 sampled primary-video frames. Independent local review covers all 17 dimensions, independently passes four SQLite regressions and an account-only cohort-parity reproduction, and records VERIFY_FINAL_EVIDENCE with no new blocking finding. Three existing minor layout observations retain owners and repair paths. All 82 files in the new evidence cohort match their published Git bytes; earlier captures and failed receipts retain their original source identities. Production build, TypeScript, focused lint, documentation/catalog validation and privacy checks pass. Full-file lint retains 22 reproduced prerequisite findings in two existing files.\n\nA separate internal publication repair raises the existing documentation generator's three Git-read buffers to a bounded 64 MiB after its file inventory exceeded the default 1 MiB. Complete inventory and validation rules remain intact. The repair is recorded separately from the 47 independently reviewed product/test bindings and passes the actual documentation commands.\n\nThis dependent draft continues to target Spatial Studio #722 on `codex/parallax-surface-orientation`. Its inspected prerequisite is `a5eeb5b42561042cea7e799a3b0d54c1b03c1006`; later prerequisite commits are not claimed as integrated. After #722 lands and the selected Crossdeck design/integration gate is cleared through its owner, reconcile the landed prerequisites, retarget this existing PR and obtain fresh ordinary exact-candidate Sounding Line capture/review and qualification. Planning against live protected main `99a2babaefbbe051de0352c4aca22c8723b743b8` still stops at the Crossdeck design obligation; dependent planning also reports unregistered consumers. Required protected journeys remain intact. No protected attestation, Mainline Decision, merge or owner acceptance is claimed.\n\n[Implementation and qualification record](https://github.com/Kgray44/treasurehuntSoT/blob/4199ad765631dcfee202f82975d154a51aacc798/Development_Docs/Projects/Project_Admiralty/AI_Economics_Capability_Intelligence_20261014.md), [new independent review](https://github.com/Kgray44/treasurehuntSoT/blob/4199ad765631dcfee202f82975d154a51aacc798/Development_Docs/Projects/Project_Admiralty/evidence/ai-economics-attempt-ratios-20261015/independent-review.json), [source and artifact integrity](https://github.com/Kgray44/treasurehuntSoT/blob/4199ad765631dcfee202f82975d154a51aacc798/Development_Docs/Projects/Project_Admiralty/evidence/ai-economics-attempt-ratios-20261015/source-artifact-integrity.json). Both earlier reviewed cohorts remain immutable. Provider-confirmed billing requires genuine provider evidence through a trusted adapter; no invoice-feed service is added.","commits":[{"authoredDate":"2026-10-15T02:35:47Z","authors":[{"email":"kkidsgray@icloud.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MzczMDEx","login":"Kgray44","name":"Kgray44"}],"committedDate":"2026-10-15T02:35:47Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"